  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trafficking in Persons, Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this program, World Vision aims to strengthen comprehensive reintegration support for victims of trafficking in Burma through a coordinated local, regional, and national approach. Objectives include improving comprehensive services for identified victims of trafficking; and creating results-driven community, subnational, national, and regional networks empowered to combat human trafficking. The program will operate in townships in Yangon, Mandalay, Ayeyarwaddy Regions, and Shan Stateall of which have either been identified as hotspots for human trafficking or areas with high levels of internal migration. This program will build off of prior anti-trafficking programs in Burma, including Trafficking in Persons (TIP) Office programming and the Australia-funded Australia-Asia Partnership against TIP, by scaling efforts to reach more survivors and further bridge the gap between local civil society and national-level government officials. This project will work with the government (central and local) and civil society organizations to help foster cooperation between the two. It will also provide some support to the government on building capacity for protection issues. This will include holding coordination workshops to which government and civil society stakeholders will be invited, and direct training on victim protection to the Department of Social Welfare as well as NGO service providers.</narrative>
  </description>
